{"id": "EUVD-2026-80423", "enisaUuid": "301cc6dc-9ddb-348a-b1b6-a36e8c4cbbff", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm: fix race between partial drm_dev_register() failure and ioctl\n\nIf drm_dev_register() fails after registering a minor (e.g. render minor\nregistered, primary minor fails), userspace could have opened the first\nminor and entered a drm_dev_enter() critical section. Since the\nunplugged flag was never set, the ioctl proceeds while the error path\ntears down device resources.\n\nFix this by introducing drm_dev_synchronize_unplug(), which sets the\nunplugged flag and waits for the SRCU barrier, ensuring all in-flight\ndrm_dev_enter() critical sections complete before cleanup proceeds; call\nit on the error path of drm_dev_register().", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:17", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26d9162213952927cd59c0d94b7e0e992b347bec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24d28d15c0f7f7d4a1c229f8730314f0f8758810", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6729990df9e70623bf53f855b521ae71ca9cb278", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0a7e2e177f2f18b9e7318a4c64ac44efd9ef22c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19dbfe4d586aecfed121cb3fa62281761d9d341f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79d09cfe90304ff4f195e47d569800f5e0f8b854", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d1215a72159d00001e08dee162e27718934bee9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb197f7d60f00d0f5b1b3505dfc86a7e36045a3e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hjv8-5wf8-79gw", "CVE-2026-89823"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18d5290e-4f0a-389f-9b73-0a7aa968d4ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "399ece7f-f5d6-39ce-ba61-15a133ceda64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":